  "title": "Should the food road show the empty-handed walking too?",
  "question": "Which of these reads better as a food road?",
  "context_md": "One choice inside the new `F7` view, on the far-larder bed. Both panes draw the same run; the only difference is whether ants walking with **nothing in their jaws** leave a mark.\n\n- one pane draws **red-orange where they walked carrying** and **blue where they walked empty**;\n- the other draws **only the carrying**.\n\nThe amber hatch — ground they took food out of — is the same in both.\n\nThis bed is the hard case on purpose: here the colony wanders a long way and hardly ever finds anything, so the empty-handed traffic is most of what there is. On the planted bed it is the other way round — nearly every step there is a laden one. **Whichever you pick becomes the default**, and the other stays available.",
